<section class="section" id="the-platform">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">Capture in the field. Act on the record. Report from the same record. <span>Four modules on one data model, from the field to the filing.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="chapters">
      <article class="chapter">
        <div class="chapter-text">
          <p class="chapter-kicker">Capture · Smart Forms &amp; Tasks, Trek</p>
          <h3 class="chapter-title">Field capture, online or offline</h3>
          <p class="chapter-lead">Timestamped, geotagged, and fully digital field capture that works offline and syncs when you're back in range.</p>
          <ul class="feature-runs feature-runs--stack">
            <li><h4>Forms that follow the answer</h4><p>A field appears only when it applies, like a leak rate after a Yes.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Filled from the registry</h4><p>Component and asset details come from the record, not retyped.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Dispatched by rule and site</h4><p>Rounds and tasks routed to the role that owns them.</p></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="chapter-links"><a class="text-action" href="/forms">See Smart Forms &amp; Tasks</a><a class="text-action" href="/trek">See Trek</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-media chapter-media--phone">
          <img src="/static/img/platform/mobile-capture-phone.webp" width="352" height="661" loading="lazy" alt="Phone showing an offline inspection round on Pipeline Segment 7 (PHMSA 192.739 valve inspection) with 4 records queued: no leakage observed, 742 psi within spec, a geotagged photo, and a Sign &amp; queue button.">
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="chapter">
        <div class="chapter-text">
          <p class="chapter-kicker">Act · Unified Asset Intelligence, Workflow Automation</p>
          <h3 class="chapter-title">Work that moves on the record</h3>
          <p class="chapter-lead">A live registry of every asset — condition, custody, and history in one record — with routing that moves findings to resolution without the email chase.</p>
          <ul class="feature-runs feature-runs--stack">
            <li><h4>Routed and escalated</h4><p>Findings go to the right role by location and escalate before the SLA breaks.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Telemetry on the asset</h4><p>SCADA, IIoT, and production readings, stored on the asset.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Outliers flagged</h4><p>An anomaly model checks each reading against its neighbors and flags the outliers for review.</p></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="chapter-links"><a class="text-action" href="/assets">See Unified Asset Intelligence</a><a class="text-action" href="/workflows">See Workflow Automation</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-media">
          <img class="chapter-screen" src="/static/img/assets/hero-asset-record-screen.webp" width="1440" height="893" loading="lazy" alt="Assetas asset record for Orcutt AGC-ENG224, an active Caterpillar CAT-3508 engine at Orcutt Hill Compressor Station: AIRS ID 123/9187/009, serial number 23701131, in service since 2006-01-15, with a photo of the engine and its QR code.">
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="chapter">
        <div class="chapter-text">
          <p class="chapter-kicker">Report · Compliance &amp; Emissions</p>
          <h3 class="chapter-title">Reports from the same record</h3>
          <p class="chapter-lead">Every asset mapped to the requirements it must satisfy — permits, 40 CFR, PHMSA, and state regulations.</p>
          <ul class="feature-runs feature-runs--stack">
            <li><h4>Calculated as data arrives</h4><p>Fuel use and run hours feed calculation groups for the GHG and state inventories.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Exported in agency formats</h4><p>Subpart W to e-GGRT and state inventories, from tracked data rather than a rebuild before the deadline.</p></li>
            <li><h4>Answers that show their sources</h4><p>The assistant works on your records and the regulatory text, and shows what it read.</p></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="chapter-links"><a class="text-action" href="/compliance">See Compliance &amp; Emissions</a><a class="text-action" href="/platform/emissions">See emissions reporting</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="chapter-media">
          <img src="/static/img/compliance/electronic-submissions.webp" width="543" height="460" loading="lazy" alt="Electronic submissions this reporting period, on track across 4 destinations and 3 formats: EPA eGGRT Subpart W submitted as XML to the agency schema, Texas state emission inventory in draft and due Mar 31, FERC Form 2 via eTariff scheduled for the Q3 filing window, and a structured agency data feed delivered as a JSON payload.">
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">Follow one finding through the record. <span>A leak at Skid A-114, from the inspection form to the rule it satisfies.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="stepper">
      <ol class="stepper-list">
        <li class="stepper-item">
          <h3 class="stepper-title"><span class="stepper-kicker">01 · Found</span> Leak logged at the relief valve</h3>
          <div class="stepper-body"><p>Started offline at 9:42 AM. The leak-rate field appears only after a Yes.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="stepper-item">
          <h3 class="stepper-title"><span class="stepper-kicker">02 · Routed</span> Escalated, then dispatched</h3>
          <div class="stepper-body"><p>Above threshold, so it goes to the supervisor and a work order queues behind it.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="stepper-item">
          <h3 class="stepper-title"><span class="stepper-kicker">03 · Recorded</span> On the skid's one record</h3>
          <div class="stepper-body"><p>Telemetry, inspections, work orders, and the asset itself in one record. No re-keying.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="stepper-item">
          <h3 class="stepper-title"><span class="stepper-kicker">04 · Mapped</span> Tied to the rule it satisfies</h3>
          <div class="stepper-body"><p>The Method 21 survey maps to NSPS OOOOb, with the citation on the record.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="stepper-stage">
        <figure class="stepper-media"><img src="/static/img/forms/hero-form-in-progress.webp" width="639" height="407" loading="lazy" alt="Leak inspection form FORM-2281 in progress for Skid A-114, relief valve RV-22, started offline at 9:42 AM: leak observed yes, estimated leak rate 42 SCFH, component auto-filled from the registry. The leak-rate field appeared automatically after answering Yes."></figure>
        <figure class="stepper-media"><img src="/static/img/forms/dispatch-workflow.webp" width="531" height="266" loading="lazy" alt="Workflow for FORM-2281: form submitted offline at 9:47 AM (done), escalated to supervisor because the leak rate is above threshold (in progress), work order dispatched (queued, waiting on escalation)."></figure>
        <figure class="stepper-media"><img src="/static/img/platform/one-data-model.webp" width="611" height="556" loading="lazy" alt="One data model: Skid A-114 at Cedar Ridge Plant. Telemetry, inspections, work orders, and assets feed one unified record, mapped to Title V, current, last synced 4 minutes ago. Capture once, prove anywhere: no re-keying. Requirement mapping: 100% of records."></figure>
        <figure class="stepper-media"><img src="/static/img/compliance/hero-requirement-mapping.webp" width="569" height="406" loading="lazy" alt="Requirement mapping: an LDAR Method 21 survey on Skid A-114 maps to the NSPS OOOOb methane rule, a berm inspection at Dry Creek Pad maps to SPCC 40 CFR 112 spill prevention, and a Title V annual report auto-drafted from readings maps to the EPA Title V operating permit. Every field record links to the exact citation it satisfies."></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

